   "importance": 5,
   "certainty": "excavated",
   "summary": "The state wing of Domitian's palace by the architect Rabirius, dedicated in 92: a colonnaded front to the Area Palatina with the Aula Regia (about 30.5 x 38.7 m, its walls once some 30 m high) in the centre between the apsed Basilica and the so-called Lararium; behind them a great peristyle with an octagonal maze-fountain, and at the rear the Cenatio Iovis, the vast dining hall with a heated floor flanked by oval nymphaea. Martial thought it touched the stars.",
   "phases": [
    {
     "y": 92,
     "t": "dedication"
    },
    {
     "y": 193,
     "t": "Pertinax killed in the palace"
    },
    {
     "y": 500,
     "t": "Theodoric restores the palace"
    }
   ],
   "sources": [
    {
     "a": "Martial",
     "w": "Epigrammata",
     "r": "8.36"
    },
