   "importance": 5,
   "certainty": "excavated",
   "summary": "The private wing of the palace, built on two levels: an upper peristyle at the level of the Domus Flavia with a pool and an island shrine, and 10 m below a lower peristyle with a fountain of Amazon shields, surrounded by vaulted suites, opening to the Circus Maximus through a great curved facade. The name derives from 'Augustus', the title of the reigning emperor.",
